From: lua-lsm-testsuite
Subject: [PATCH] run_qemu_anolis: add QEMU_PIDFILE env knob

The harness needs a deterministic way to identify the QEMU child PID for
clean shutdown when a cell reaches its boot-timeout. Without -pidfile, the
launcher script's PID is the only handle the harness has, and signalling it
sometimes leaves a zombie qemu-system-x86_64 holding the host SSH port,
which then breaks the next cell.

Add an optional QEMU_PIDFILE env var; when set, pass `-pidfile <path>` to
QEMU. Default empty preserves existing behaviour.

This patch is shipped separately from the harness so it can be merged into
DebugKernel on its own schedule.

---
 run_qemu_anolis.sh | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/run_qemu_anolis.sh b/run_qemu_anolis.sh
--- a/run_qemu_anolis.sh
+++ b/run_qemu_anolis.sh
@@ -136,6 +136,8 @@ ROOT_DEV="${ROOT_DEV:-/dev/vda}"
 CONSOLE="${CONSOLE:-ttyS0}"
 KERNEL_CMDLINE="${KERNEL_CMDLINE:-}"
 EXTRA_CMDLINE="${EXTRA_CMDLINE:-}"
 QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS="${QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS:-}"
+QEMU_PIDFILE="${QEMU_PIDFILE:-}"

 ENABLE_GDB="${ENABLE_GDB:-0}"
 GDB_PORT="${GDB_PORT:-1235}"
@@ -274,6 +276,12 @@ if [[ "${DEBUG_WAIT}" == "1" ]]; then
     QEMU_ARGS+=(-S)
 fi

+if [[ -n "${QEMU_PIDFILE}" ]]; then
+    QEMU_ARGS+=(-pidfile "${QEMU_PIDFILE}")
+fi
+
 if [[ -n "${QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS}" ]]; then
     read -r -a QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS_ARR <<< "${QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS}"
     QEMU_ARGS+=("${QEMU_EXTRA_ARGS_ARR[@]}")
--
